 loc='\U0001f4cd Near Anloo / Gasteren \u00b7 Heath and woodland \u00b7 Medium-sized',
 desc='The <b>Groote Veld</b> near Anloo is exactly what the name says: the great common <b>veld</b> of the marke, the sweeping heath where the village sheep grazed and where farmers cut their sods. Until well into the nineteenth century such commons covered most of Drenthe \u2014 an <b>open, treeless landscape</b> that travellers described as monotonous and even frightening. After the Marken Act most of it was divided and planted, and what you see here is the mixed outcome: <b>heath remnants alternating with Scots pine wood</b>, and dense scrub of juniper and birch on the transitions. In recent decades part of the woodland has been <b>converted back to heath</b>, to restore the historic character of the common and give heath fauna room. It works: <b>nightjar, woodlark and stonechat</b> are present, and the <b>sand lizard</b> hunts on the warm sandy patches. Burial mounds and old field tracks also lie within the area.',
